@startuml Enemy AI Turn - Communication Diagram
!theme plain
title **UC-5: Enemy AI Turn – Communication Diagram**

object ":GameEngine" as engine #LightCoral
object ":GameController" as ctrl #LightGreen
object ":EnemyAI" as ai #Thistle
object ":MoveAction" as ma #LightYellow
object ":MoveEffect" as me #Orange
object ":GameSession" as sess #White
object ":Hero" as hero #Pink
object ":Enemy (Knight)" as enemy #Red
object ":Map" as map #LightGray
object ":GridCell" as cell #LightGray

engine -- sess
engine -- ai
engine -- ctrl
ai -- sess
ai -- hero
ai -- enemy
ai -- ma
ctrl -- ma
ctrl -- me
ctrl -- sess
ma -- sess
ma -- hero
ma -- map
ma -- me
map -- cell
me -- enemy

engine -> sess : 1: getEnemies()
engine -> ai : 2: decideAction(enemy, session)
ai -> sess : 2.1: getHero()
ai -> hero : 2.2: getRow(), getCol()
ai -> enemy : 2.3: getRow(), getCol()
ai -> ma : 2.4: <<create>> MoveAction(dRow, dCol)
engine -> ctrl : 3: executeAction(action)
ctrl -> ma : 3.1: resolve(session)
ma -> sess : 3.1.1: getHero()
ma -> hero : 3.1.2: getRow(), getCol()
ma -> sess : 3.1.3: getMap()
ma -> map : 3.1.4: getCell(newRow, newCol)
ma -> cell : 3.1.5: isWalkable()
ma -> me : 3.1.6: <<create>> MoveEffect(enemy, newRow, newCol)
ctrl -> me : 3.2: apply(session)
me -> enemy : 3.2.1: setPosition(newRow, newCol)
ctrl -> sess : 3.3: advanceTurn()

note bottom of engine
  **GRASP Controller**: GameController handles execution.
  **Polymorphism**: MoveAction works for both Hero and Enemy.
  **Low Coupling**: EnemyAI only creates Actions, not Effects.
  **High Cohesion**: AI logic is separated from game loop.
  **Indirection**: GameEngine delegates to EnemyAI for decisions
  and to GameController for execution.
end note

@enduml
